Z||000000||Harry||01-31-2000||12:29 AM||||Well my cherry has been broken now for shure!<BR>The clutch transplant has been a success with  the exception of a couple broken vacumm lines (you know the hard plastic ones under the intake).<BR>Does any one know of anywhere these can be purchased new?<BR>PS all you clutch life hating people should know my car now shifts like it's brand new again......To sweet, good luck to all fixing their's. ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-31-2000||04:39 AM||||Harry--Your tail light kit is done, just waiting on $$ and an address.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||01-31-2000||04:02 PM||||I know what you mean.  I put a centerforce dual friction in my GT and it works great.  All the hydraulic parts are new also.  <P>You may want to check a junk yard for those hard vacuum lines.  I couldn't even begin to imagine what a new set would cost.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BOILERMAKER||01-31-2000||04:20 PM||||I actually called my local dealer about a set of those new hard hoses and they told me that they were discontinued.  Isn't that lovely!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||01-31-2000||09:08 PM||||LOOK GUYS GO TO YOUR AUTO PARTS STORE,then buy some hose,5/32 i think, then break off your original vacuam lines, a little after where they connect, thEn put the hose in the original line and connect it back up. Remember, break it off after each connection that way you use the oiginal connector but with new hose in back. i hope you guys understand this, cause that's what i did to my lines and it works great, good luck, AL. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||01-31-2000||09:08 PM||||LOOK GUYS GO TO YOUR AUTO PARTS STORE,then buy some hose,5/32 i think, then break off your original vacuam lines, a little after where they connect, thEn put the hose in the original line and connect it back up. Remember, break it off after each connection that way you use the oiginal connector but with new hose in back. i hope you guys understand this, cause that's what i did to my lines and it works great, good luck, AL. ||||reg||14
Z||000006||ka4nkf||01-31-2000||10:16 PM||||If you have to have some of those hard lines, i saw them at advance auto. they come in a package of so many feet and size, price was not bad either.||||reg||1
